{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For HaShem had firmly shut.</b> This is a closing up of orifices, great and small, and therefore the doubled expression. 'Every womb' — this is the stopping of birth, and it includes all females among humans, beasts, and every living creature; and so our Rabbis of blessed memory said: even a hen in the house of Avimelekh did not lay her egg. And in this verse the king's affliction and that of his entire household is specified, for until now the parashah did not mention it and we did not know with what he was stricken. And it did not mention the affliction by the name Avimelekh, just as it mentioned the healing by his name — 'and Elohim healed Avimelekh' — but this is in order to show honor to kingship, and as a matter of propriety and respect for Sarah, that the Torah did not mention it thus:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:52.806777850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}